    "author_association": "COLLABORATOR",
    "body": "Ah yes, this is expected in the tutorial. For a more robust matmul you can refer to https://github.com/openai/triton/blob/master/python/triton/ops/matmul.py\r\n\r\nLook in particular at the following lines\r\n```\r\n        if META['EVEN_K']:\r\n            a = tl.load(A)\r\n            b = tl.load(B)\r\n        else:\r\n            a = tl.load(A, mask=rk[None, :] < k, other=0.)\r\n            b = tl.load(B, mask=rk[:, None] < k, other=0.)\r\n```\r\nin the tutorials it's not there, which means that the kernel will accumulate out-of-bounds memory elements when K isn't a multiple of BLOCK_K",
    "created_at": "2021-08-05T17:01:52Z",
